g directories the daemon finds (brief scope item 2). Suggested config location and shape: <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json (config.Dir()) holding {\"projects\": [\"/abs/root\", ...]}, path overridable via --registry (TASK-2's flag) — the brief leaves the location open, confirm the choice while implementing. Each entry validated as an existing directory (a registered project needs docs/ for jobs, but only warn on that — a root without docs/ lists no jobs rather than failing startup). Registrations are read once at startup; changing the file means editing and restarting (v1). Provide Projects() (ordered copy) and a Project(name) lookup so every handler resolves ONLY against registered roots — the single choke point TASK-7's zero-path-inputs enforcement builds on. Include registry_test.go: parses the config, validates roots, rejects a missing file (empty registry, not an error), rejects non-directory entries, lookup by exact path and by base name.\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/wood_listener-architecture/implementation.md:\n  Line 27: `Registry` type: loads an explicit config file (`<checkout>/config/serve.json`,\n\n\n/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/extension_settings-layout/session.log:\n  Line 3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1787919295387,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7b4a8d5ffeJWKjfWHud2qnLO\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_00_acJWCJdDyJs2tFItqynQ2594\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/brief.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/extension_settings-layout/brief.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Brief: settings layout\\n2: \\n3: status: open\\n4: type: fix\\n5: id: extension\\n6: branch: fix/extension_settings-layout\\n7: date: 2026-08-28\\n8: author: Leander Muskalla\\n9: \\n10: ## What\\n11: \\n12: Let us improve the settings layout of mg tui.\\n13: It used to be fine, but we've added more and more settings and now it's quite hard t