:\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_40b9cd540c934c959191e4a6\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md\",\"limit\":40,\"offset\":45},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/project-template/docs/AGENTS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n45: and declare a network isolation level (`network:`); both are designed but not\\n46: yet enforced. `docs/agent-template.md` in the manigot checkout is a copy-me\\n47: reference agent showing the full frontmatter surface and every guardrail.\\n48: Every job-worktree session ends with a host-side sweep-commit of leftover\\n49: changes (a `[<id>] chore: commit all` commit), so read-only agents' outputs\\n50: (like the analyst's tasks.md) are committed after their session and `mg done`\\n51: is never blocked by uncommitted leftovers. The sweep never runs for plain\\n52: sessions, `mg host` sessions, or any `--job` resolution that stays on the main\\n53: worktree — the flat-scan fallback (a repo with no local branches, or a\\n54: non-git project — there is no job worktree to sweep) and a pre-worktree job\\n55: (its branch still checked out in the main worktree itself) alike — since the\\n56: main project root holds the user's own uncommitted work.\\n57: Agent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\\n58: session git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\\n59: pushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\\n60: The manigot TUI's job detail view also offers a `t` key that opens the job's\\n61: branch diff in tig (`mg diff <job> --tig`) in a tmux split pane / new\\n62: terminal, gated on tig being installed on the host, and an `l` key that\\n63: tails the job's mg-jdi `run.log` live in a tmux split pane / new terminal,\\n64: gated on a run.log existing for the job.\\n65: `mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a read-only control...\n  Line 359: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\