o as it happens, distinct from the log tab...\n  Line 435: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1787921067292,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7999c4fffe1anLtOEgzjXUGJ\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_00_Aks2OZLaeuqLCi24Beo13950\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/brief.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/guest_fix-tailing/brief.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Brief: Fix tailing\\n2: \\n3: status: open\\n4: type: fix\\n5: id: guest\\n6: branch: fix/guest_fix-tailing\\n7: date: 2026-08-28\\n8: author: Leander Muskalla\\n9: \\n10: ## What\\n11: \\n12: When I try the new tail feature in a job detail view, it shows no stream. It seems buffered, so I'd get exactly what I get in the log view. No tail at all, no improvement.\\n13: I'm currently using opencode, so as I understood it, opencode does support tailing.\\n14: Check if we're actually grabbing the output or not.\\n15: Also, there should be a difference between the log (agent invoked, agent result, next agent invoked, etc.) and tailing. The full tail should also be written to a log, but to a different one, a more verbose one.\\n16: \\n17: ## Why\\n18: \\n19: <!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\\n20: \\n21: ## Out of scope\\n22: \\n23: <!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\\n24: \\n25: ## Notes\\n26: \\n27: <!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\\n\\n(End of file - total 27 lines)\\n</content>\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\\n# manigot\\n\\nIsolated agent environment per project: one Docker image, subscription\\nbilling via mounted OAuth credentials, real filesystem containment, and a\\nstructured brief → tasks → implementation → verdict job workflow. Runs a\\nsession under a subscription profile — the built-ins `claude-pro` (Claude\\nCode, billed to Claude Pro/Max), `zai` (OpenCode, billed to a Z.AI Coding\\nPlan), `opencode-go` (OpenCode, billed to the OpenCode Go subscription),\\n`opencode-zen` (OpenCode, bill...\n  Line 485: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1787921162404,\"sessionID\":\"ses_fb7999c4fffe1anLtOEgzjXUGJ\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_7a074f4a989e434ba980773d\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git diff main...HEAD -- scripts/entrypoint.sh README.md project-template/docs/AGENTS.md docs/ROADMAP.md docs/AGENTS.md\"},\"output\":\"diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex a8263bd..98ef682 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -862,12 +862,13 @@ no separate configuration needed there.\\n output to its own terminal as each invocation completes, and rings the\\n terminal bell when it stops. Every invocation's raw step-level output — the\\n whole blow-by-blow of tool calls and intermediate messages, not just the\\n-final answer — is also persisted to the job's own `session.log`\\n-(`docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log`), so what an agent did during an\\n-unattended run survives and rides the job's branch into the archive\\n-(rendering/tailing it is a separate, later feature). A TUI-launched run (see\\n-below) has no terminal of its own at all — the list's status badge and the\\n-detail view's log tab are how you watch it there instead.\\n+final answer — is also streamed live into the job's own `session.log`\\n+(`docs/jobs/<id>_<slug>/session.log`) as the invocation runs, so what an\\n+agent did during an unattended run survives and rides the job's branch into\\n+the archive (the TUI's `l` key tails it live — see below). A TUI-launched\\n+run (see below) has no terminal of its own at all — the list's status badge,\\n+the detail view's log tab, and the `l` tail are how you watch it there\\n+instead.\\n \\n **Getting notified.** When `mg jdi` runs unattended on a VPS, you don't want\\n to watch the terminal for it to stop. Set `NTFY_TOPIC` in `manigot/.env`\\n@@ -982,7 +983,7 @@ Detail view:\\n | `x` / `del` | permanently delete the job — shows an in-TUI confirmation (with a dirty-worktree warning when the job's worktree has uncommitted changes), then runs the in-process de...","metadata":{"matches":20,"truncated":false},"title":"serve\\.json","time":{"start":1787938537452,"end":1787938537458}},"id":"prt_04970fec8001xxMXDGyOzPNgSE","sessionID":"ses_fb68f715dffenWbrsP50CKBzBA","messageID":"msg_04970f9370016ioRSvM0tJIsda"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1787938537495,"sessionID":"ses_fb68f715dffenWbrsP50CKBzBA","part":{"id":"prt_049710013001CjMziAAbM99xus","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"","messageID":"msg_04970f9370016ioRSvM0tJIsda","sessionID":"ses_fb68f715dffenWbrsP50CKBzBA","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":68346,"input":128,"output":122,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":68096}},"cost":0.000585352}}
