age main — the health endpoint needs it), enforces the bind/auth startup guard (TASK-6), then blocks on the serve loop and shuts down gracefully on SIGINT/SIGTERM (http.Server.Shutdown with a bounded drain). Long-running-process lifecycle is new territory for the single binary — the signal-handling and shutdown path must be testable (an httptest-able Serve/Shutdown seam, not a bare http.ListenAndServe call in main).\n     files: src/cmd/mg/main.go, src/cmd/mg/serve.go (new), src/cmd/mg/serve_test.go (new)\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-3, TASK-6 (wires them; can be stubbed against their signatures and landed last among the code tasks)\n     risk: medium — blocking serve + graceful shutdown is a new process shape for mg; the shutdown drain must be bounded so a hung request cannot wedge the exit","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/wood_listener-architecture/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: listener architecture\n\nid: wood\nstatus: open\nanalyst: wood\ndate: 2026-08-27\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: Project registry in a new daemon package. Add a new internal package for the daemon (suggested name src/internal/serve — the home for the registry, HTTP server, handlers, auth, audit and locks; one package for all of it, mirroring how internal/session owns the launcher). Registry type: loads an explicit config file of project roots at startup — NO scanning, NO auto-adopting directories the daemon finds (brief scope item 2). Suggested config location and shape: <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json (config.Dir()) holding {\"projects\": [\"/abs/root\", ...]}, path overridable via --registry (TASK-2's flag) — the brief leaves the location open, confirm the choice while implementing. Each entry validated as an existing directory (a registered project needs docs/ for jobs, but only warn on that — a root without docs/ lists no jobs rather than failing startup). Registrations are r