{"type":"text","timestamp":1787938717296,"sessionID":"ses_fb68f715dffenWbrsP50CKBzBA","part":{"id":"prt_04973a1ff0014B638ScNYvlFb3","messageID":"msg_049739409001Xmi2rLzJ72ub1k","sessionID":"ses_fb68f715dffenWbrsP50CKBzBA","type":"text","text":"Analysis complete. I've written the task breakdown to `tasks.md` for job `dozen` (change config structure for mg serve). Grounded in the actual sources: `src/internal/serve/registry.go`, `api.go`, `src/cmd/mg/serve.go`, all six serve test files, `docs/AGENTS.md`, `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md`, `docs/listener.md`, and `README.md`.\n\n## Task list\n\n- **TASK-1** — Rework the registry schema in `registry.go`: `{\"projects\": [{\"name\",\"path\"}, ...]}`, `name` required, refuse-to-start validation (non-empty, single URL-safe segment reusing `validSegment`'s discipline, unique names, existing-dir path), flat-string form now fails to parse (no back-compat). *Medium risk — the core change rippling to every consumer.*\n- **TASK-2** — `Registry.Project` resolves by configured name only; exact-path/base-name/ambiguous-base-name paths removed; expose name+path pairs for the API. *Low risk.*\n- **TASK-3** — `api.go`: `projectRow.Name` from the configured value, not `filepath.Base`; update the stale resolution comment. *Low risk.*\n- **TASK-4** — Rewrite `registry_test.go` for the object schema + new validation pins (empty/slashy/traversal/non-URL-safe/duplicate names, flat-form refusal, name-only lookup). *Medium risk — proves the refusal-to-start discipline.*\n- **TASK-5** — Update all endpoint/auth/security/credentials tests (~25 `&Registry{projects: ...}` constructions + `filepath.Base(root)` URL usages) to named entries via a shared helper; verify `cmd/mg/serve_test.go` unaffected. *Medium risk — large mechanical surface.*\n- **TASK-6** — Update `mg serve` flag-help usage text in `serve.go` to the object schema. *Low risk.*\n- **TASK-7** — Docs: `docs/AGENTS.md` listener section, `project-template/docs/AGENTS.md` (hard-rule sync), `docs/listener.md`, verify `README.md` (~line 1168). *Low risk.*\n- **TASK-8** — Final verification: `go build`/`go vet`/`go test` for `internal/serve` + `cmd/mg`. *Low risk — the gate.*\n\n## Decision points flagged (not guessed)\n\n1. **\"URL-safe charset\"** — the brief's wording is open; I scoped it as `validSegment` structural checks plus a conservative URL-safe set (recommended `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`), to be documented in code.\n2. **Duplicate paths** — the old code silently collapsed them; with named entries the behavior needs an explicit decision (collapse vs. refuse), pinned by a test. Duplicate *names* are always a refusal.\n3. **`docs/listener.md`** currently contains no schema example (the brief names it for updating) — flagged to add one rather than only fix stale text.\n4. **`README.md`** isn't in the brief's explicit docs list but carries the same flat-schema example — included as \"verify/update\".\n\nNo render report exists for this job (pure Go CLI work, no frontend). No `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT:` — the job is fully scoped and implementable from these tasks.","time":{"start":1787938710015,"end":1787938717294}}}
