{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQGncoJ7nYeFNGkeKEQuWM","type":"tool_result","content":"1140\t  currently running agent's blow-by-blow live; `tail -f` idles harmlessly\n1141\t  once a run ends, and you end the pane with Ctrl+C like any tail.\n1142\t\n1143\t**Notification.** A direct `mg jdi --job <id>` run rings the terminal bell\n1144\titself when it stops (see [Autonomous mode](#autonomous-mode-mg-jdi)). A\n1145\t`j`-launched run has no terminal to ring into, so the TUI rings it instead,\n1146\ton its own next poll, the first time it notices that job's status turn into\n1147\t`finished` or `needs human` — once per fresh stop, not on every poll while\n1148\tit stays stopped, and never for a job that was already stopped before this\n1149\tTUI session started watching it.\n1150\t\n1151\t---\n1152\t\n1153\t## Listener\n1154\t\n1155\t`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a **read-only**\n1156\tcontrol API over a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a\n1157\tnative GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or\n1158\tfrom a VPS. It is job one of the control-plane sequence; the API is read-only\n1159\tby design (mutating endpoints, live run supervision with streamed logs, and\n1160\tany frontend are later jobs — see the out-of-scope list in\n1161\t[`docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md`](docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md)).\n1162\t\n1163\t**Registry.** An explicit config file of project roots — no scanning, no\n1164\tauto-adopting directories the daemon finds:\n1165\t\n1166\t```bash\n1167\t# <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json  (override with --registry)\n1168\t{\"projects\": [\"/abs/project/root\", ...]}\n1169\t```\n1170\t\n1171\tRegistrations are read once at startup; changing them means editing the file\n1172\tand restarting (v1). Each entry must be an existing directory; a root without\n1173\t`docs/` is accepted and simply lists no jobs.\n1174\t\n1175\t**Binding + auth.** The daemon binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default and is\n1176\ttokenless in that shape — the machine's own user is the trust boundary, as it\n1177\tis for the CLI. A non-loopback bind (a VPS) **requires** a bearer token —\n1178\t`--token`, else `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN` — or the daemon refuses to start; there is\n1179\tno flag that turns that guard off. When a token is configured, every request\n1180\tmust carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (compared in constant time); a\n1181\tmissing or wrong token is a `401`. TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy /\n1182\tnginx) — the daemon always serves plain HTTP and never terminates TLS, the\n1183\tonly safe posture behind a proxy. A token without TLS is no protection.\n1184\t\n1185\t**API.** `GET /health` (version, docker image present, per-profile\n1186\treadiness), `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/<p>/jobs` (id / status / stage /\n1187\ttype / date / title, plus per-job mg-jdi state),\n1188\t`GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/<brief|tasks|implementation|verdict>`\n1189\t(raw markdown), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/jdi` (status + `run.log` +"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0a07b2b-e4d4-47fe-bb0c-9b7aa946ef87","uuid":"7b8d80ba-768f-4cfb-a7c9-943dce9db70b","timestamp":"2026-08-28T17:48:34.738Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","content":"  currently running agent's blow-by-blow live; `tail -f` idles harmlessly\n  once a run ends, and you end the pane with Ctrl+C like any tail.\n\n**Notification.** A direct `mg jdi --job <id>` run rings the terminal bell\nitself when it stops (see [Autonomous mode](#autonomous-mode-mg-jdi)). A\n`j`-launched run has no terminal to ring into, so the TUI rings it instead,\non its own next poll, the first time it notices that job's status turn into\n`finished` or `needs human` — once per fresh stop, not on every poll while\nit stays stopped, and never for a job that was already stopped before this\nTUI session started watching it.\n\n---\n\n## Listener\n\n`mg serve` is the listener: a long-running daemon exposing a **read-only**\ncontrol API over a registry of project roots, so any surface — a web UI, a\nnative GUI, a future CLI — can attach to it as a client, from localhost or\nfrom a VPS. It is job one of the control-plane sequence; the API is read-only\nby design (mutating endpoints, live run supervision with streamed logs, and\nany frontend are later jobs — see the out-of-scope list in\n[`docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md`](docs/jobs/wood_listener-architecture/brief.md)).\n\n**Registry.** An explicit config file of project roots — no scanning, no\nauto-adopting directories the daemon finds:\n\n```bash\n# <manigot checkout>/config/serve.json  (override with --registry)\n{\"projects\": [\"/abs/project/root\", ...]}\n```\n\nRegistrations are read once at startup; changing them means editing the file\nand restarting (v1). Each entry must be an existing directory; a root without\n`docs/` is accepted and simply lists no jobs.\n\n**Binding + auth.** The daemon binds `127.0.0.1:8080` by default and is\ntokenless in that shape — the machine's own user is the trust boundary, as it\nis for the CLI. A non-loopback bind (a VPS) **requires** a bearer token —\n`--token`, else `$MG_SERVE_TOKEN` — or the daemon refuses to start; there is\nno flag that turns that guard off. When a token is configured, every request\nmust carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (compared in constant time); a\nmissing or wrong token is a `401`. TLS is the reverse proxy's job (Caddy /\nnginx) — the daemon always serves plain HTTP and never terminates TLS, the\nonly safe posture behind a proxy. A token without TLS is no protection.\n\n**API.** `GET /health` (version, docker image present, per-profile\nreadiness), `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/<p>/jobs` (id / status / stage /\ntype / date / title, plus per-job mg-jdi state),\n`GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/files/<brief|tasks|implementation|verdict>`\n(raw markdown), `GET /projects/<p>/jobs/<j>/jdi` (status + `run.log` +","numLines":50,"startLine":1140,"totalLines":1222}}}
